{"id":47396,"ord":108,"n_segments":152,"prev":47395,"next":47397,"doc":{"id":"61125","title":"61125_Teddy Bunn oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Theodore Leroy Bunn","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/61125/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=61125"},"chapter":"Noone, Kirby and family","title":"Jimmy Noone Orchestra on Decca; Noone's background","category":"recording_session","summary":"They play Noone records, and Bunn says Noone was a New Orleans musician whose smooth style sounded like clarinet study.","period":"late 1930s","year_from":1937,"year_to":1939,"words":422,"start":[200,10],"end":[204,3],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=61125#s47396","tags":{"places":[{"name":"New Orleans","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"Chicago","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"Louisiana","focus":0,"type":"state"}],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Jimmy Noone Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Jimmy Noone"}]},"people":[{"name":"Jimmy Noone","qid":"Q492247","n":4},{"name":"Red McKenzie","qid":"Q1600338","n":2},{"name":"Frankie Newton","qid":"Q1445089","n":1},{"name":"Frank Smith","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"O'Neil Spencer","qid":"Q2043379","n":1},{"name":"Teddy Simmons","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":30,"theme_name":"The reed and horn player's craft: clarinet, sax, tone","community":71,"community_name":"Who were the great clarinetists? Favorites and rivals","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":200,"b":10,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"This is the Jimmy Noone Orchestra."},{"p":200,"b":11,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":200,"b":12,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"On Decca."},{"p":200,"b":13,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"And I'm on guitar there."},{"p":200,"b":14,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Oh, yeah. There's a vocal, too. I don't know who it is."},{"p":200,"b":15,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Huh?"},{"p":200,"b":16,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"There'll be a vocal coming up. I'm not sure who it is."},{"p":200,"b":17,"s":"","x":"(O'Neil Spencer or Teddy Simmons - ed.)"},{"p":200,"b":18,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Who's that?"},{"p":200,"b":19,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"I don't know."},{"p":201,"b":0,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Red McKenzie?"},{"p":201,"b":1,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"No, it's not Red McKenzie. What did you think of Red McKenzie?"},{"p":201,"b":2,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"All right."},{"p":201,"b":3,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Yeah. Jimmy Noone was a very pretty player."},{"p":201,"b":4,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":201,"b":5,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"He had a real nice --"},{"p":201,"b":6,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":201,"b":7,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"-- smooth style. Did he have some classical training? Because I notice --"},{"p":201,"b":8,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"He's out of that school."},{"p":201,"b":9,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Yeah. Because I notice on, you know, 'Apex Blues'?"},{"p":201,"b":10,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":201,"b":11,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"He does a whole riff that sounds like a study, you know, like a school --"},{"p":201,"b":12,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"School of study."},{"p":201,"b":13,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Like something he might have done in school and he adapted it."},{"p":201,"b":14,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah, he probably did."},{"p":201,"b":15,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Yeah. He's from Chicago?"},{"p":201,"b":16,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":201,"b":17,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Wasn't he from Chicago?"},{"p":201,"b":18,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah. His home is -- wasn't it in a"},{"p":202,"b":0,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"southern state?"},{"p":202,"b":1,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Tennessee?"},{"p":202,"b":2,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"No."},{"p":202,"b":3,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Farther down?"},{"p":202,"b":4,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Huh?"},{"p":202,"b":5,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Farther south?"},{"p":202,"b":6,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":202,"b":7,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"I don't know. Mississippi? Alabama?"},{"p":202,"b":8,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"No."},{"p":202,"b":9,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Louisiana?"},{"p":202,"b":10,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Louisiana."},{"p":202,"b":11,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"He was from Louisiana?"},{"p":202,"b":12,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":202,"b":13,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"From New Orleans or from --"},{"p":202,"b":14,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"New Orleans."},{"p":202,"b":15,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Was he a New Orleans musician?"},{"p":202,"b":16,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":202,"b":17,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"I didn't know that."},{"p":202,"b":18,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":202,"b":19,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"That's interesting, because that's a -- you know, \"Sweet Lorraine\" is an actual like, a song, like a typical pop type song in a way."},{"p":202,"b":20,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":202,"b":21,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"You've got the blues thing, even when you play a tune."},{"p":203,"b":0,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":203,"b":1,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"You tend to put those blues interpretations."},{"p":203,"b":2,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah. That's Jimmy Noone."},{"p":203,"b":3,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Yeah. Well that explains the kind of French -- when I listened to this tape the other night --"},{"p":203,"b":4,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":203,"b":5,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"-- I was thinking this sounds like -- yeah -- this sounds like a French clarinet study."},{"p":203,"b":6,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":203,"b":7,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Like a classical practice routine, like an etude, you know?"},{"p":203,"b":8,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah. This one."},{"p":203,"b":9,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Yeah. Who do you think that was?"},{"p":203,"b":10,"s":"","x":"(Frank Smith, piano -- ed.)"},{"p":203,"b":11,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"I can't think of his name now, but I know him."},{"p":203,"b":12,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"It's a nice organization."},{"p":203,"b":13,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":203,"b":14,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"A nice feeling."},{"p":203,"b":15,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"How about that?"},{"p":203,"b":16,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"That's the end of that side. This is called \"Bump It\"?"},{"p":203,"b":17,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah."},{"p":203,"b":18,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"Or \"Apex Blues\". Was this like a Jimmy Noone specialty, or --"},{"p":204,"b":0,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"Yeah. \"Bump It,\""},{"p":204,"b":1,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"For his orchestra. Was there a dance to it or something like that?"},{"p":204,"b":2,"s":"MR. BUNN","x":"No."},{"p":204,"b":3,"s":"MR. ROSENBERG","x":"No. I'm going to leave this tune playing, but I think we'll maybe cut off the interview for (Interruption) awhile, and take a rest. I did want to ask you one question. When we played the Frankie Newton stuff earlier?"}]}